    {
      "path": "e2e/d9ar/cards.spec.ts",
      "content": "This check passes without checking any figures when no Stop/Target labels match, and it never inspects the price chart's current `.mark-label`. Thus a missing AXIO line label or an incorrect displayed Mark escapes the promised chart/readout coverage. Assert the expected labels for fixtures that have these lines, assert that numeric labels actually parse, and compare the current price-chart Mark with the readout (and current card). Apply a parsed-figure assertion to the P\u0026L labels too: `drawn.length \u003e 0` alone does not ensure the inner numeric assertions run.",
      "existing_code": "  const lines = await scope.locator('svg.price-strip text').evaluateAll((texts) =\u003e texts.map((t) =\u003e t.textContent ?? '').filter((t) =\u003e /^(Stop|Target) \\$/.test(t)));\n  for (const text of lines) for (const figure of figuresIn(text)) expect(plan.includes(figure), `${where}: the price chart's \"${text}\" is in the Plan block`).toBe(true);",
      "start_line": 30,
      "end_line": 31,
      "category": "test",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "e2e/d9ar/cards.spec.ts",
      "content": "BREN only validates synchronization at indices 0 and 8; the eight-key seek skips all intermediate assertions and the test never checks sessions 9 and 10. The requested first-to-last traversal applies to R-BREN-U as well as AXIO/CORV, so intermediate or final-session card regressions can pass. Step through all 11 sessions with `expectCardsAt` after each step, retaining the sale-specific crossing assertion at index 8.",
      "existing_code": "    await seek(page, scope, 'ArrowRight', 8);\n    await expectCardsAt(page, scope, 8, 11, 'BREN Thu 11-12');",
